   "meta": {
    "application": "BambuStudio-02.06.01.55",
    "profile_title": "(Optimized for PLA silk) 88g, 2h11m!",
    "profile_notes": "This is the Large 10-Pointed Star Fidget , a print-in-place sensory toy designed for a mesmerizing visual effect. It is a spinning decagram made of many interlocking rings that expand and collapse smoothly. Visual & Mechanical Design The model features a central vertical handle used for spinning and 26 concentric rings. It is designed to be print-in-place, meaning it is printed as one solid piece with no assembly required. When you pick it up, the rings drop down to create a 3D star shape that moves rhythmically. Optimized Print Settings This profile is precisely tuned for Silk PLA , which is shinier but can be trickier to print than standard plastic. Strength & Durability: It uses 3 Wall Loops and 10% Gyroid Infill . This makes the rings strong enough to handle constant fidgeting without snapping. Preventing Fused Parts: The Elephant Foot Compensation (0.15 mm) and 0.24 mm Layer Height are critical. They ensure the bottom of the rings don't squish together and get stuck to the floor. Surface Quality: The Outer Wall Width (0.74 mm) is set extra wide. This gives the Silk filament a larger surface area to catch the light, making the star look more metallic and vibrant. Printing Requirements Build Plate: A Textured PEI Plate is recommended for the best grip. Supports: No supports are needed for the rings, but the tall center handle requires a stable, level bed to prevent wobbling during the 2-hour print. Material: Best printed in Silk PLA for the intended shimmer effect as the rings move.",
